    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d897-a2">

                <pb facs="1074" n="978" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg978"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 418—Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Day.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1898-06-07"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 7,
                    1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>In obedience to your instructions, I have seen Lord Tweeddale. He sees no way to
                    take our telegrams in face of formal prohibition of Spanish Government. Spain
                    has refused his offer to take dispatches of both sides. He could suggest no
                    means of getting over the Spanish prohibition, except our guaranteeing the
                    company against all resulting losses, including forfeiture of concession.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">* * * * * * *</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hay.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
